  "question": {
    "text": "Water from a tap emerges vertically downwards with an initial speed of <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1.0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> . The cross <math><mo>-</mo></math> sectional area of the tap is <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> . Assume that the pressure is constant throughout the stream of water and that the flow is streamlined. The cross <math><mo>-</mo></math> sectional area of the stream, <math><mn>0.15</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> below the tap would be:<br />(Take <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> )"
